"event_title"} "Small-Bore Rifle, Prone, 50 metres, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "20 August 2004"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/807"} "Olympiako Kentro Skopovolis Markopoulou, Markopoulo"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/51997"} "46 from 34 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "American " [:a {:href "/athletes/104767"} "Matt Emmons"] " was the 2002 World Champion and was the favorite. In April 2004 he discovered that his small-bore rifle had been sabotaged by somebody with a screwdriver. Borrowing a gun from his training partner, Amber Darland, he used that gun to win gold in this event in Athina. Belarusian " [:a {:href "/athletes/41348"} "Sergey Martnov"] " placed third, repeating his bronze medal finish from Sydney. Two days after this event, going for a historical prone/3-position double, Emmons was leading the small-bore three positions event going into the last shot of the final when he cross-fired, hitting the wrong target, and dropped to last place among the finalists. After that event, Czech rifle shooter " [:a {:href "/athletes/104664"} "Kateřina Kůrková"] " came over to console Emmons. They eventually fell in love and married in the Czech Republic in June 2007."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Preliminary Round"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2281"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/104767"} "Matt Emmons"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "599 (1)"] [:td {} "703.3 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:cla